Review this commit range against its plan. You are a fresh session, read-only and report-only.

Plan: {{PLAN}}
Commit range: {{RANGE}}
Worktree (your cwd): {{WORKTREE}}

Check the diff of exactly that range (git diff {{RANGE}}) against the plan's Aim and Acceptance. List each finding as a numbered line (file, what is wrong, why it matters), then a line `PROBLEMS: N` with the number of findings (`PROBLEMS: 0` when there are none). The count is compared with the previous review of this job, so a finding is one distinct problem.
If the range is empty or invalid, end with STATUS: BLOCKED no commit range.
Your reply is the verdict; the dispatcher saves it to {{VERDICT_FILE}}. Do not write that file yourself. Your whole reply is saved and given to the executor that fixes the range. Last line: STATUS: PASS or STATUS: FAIL (a FAIL without a PROBLEMS line counts as no verdict).
